{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"structural_monotony\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The document does contain repeated section shapes, but the annotator supplied no evidence. Multiple body paragraphs follow a similar topic-sentence-plus-elaboration pattern, so the conclusion is plausible but unsubstantiated in the audit.\",\"evidence\":[\"A major priority was strengthening the links between research and industry.\",\"The body also considered how Australia could respond to technological change.\",\"Another area of work was the availability of finance for innovative ventures.\",\"Regional participation remained an important theme.\"]},{\"id\":\"tonal_uniformity\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The formal policy register appears consistent across the document, but the annotator gave no evidence. Because this is a whole-document judgment, it needed support from multiple parts of the text.\",\"evidence\":[\"Its work combined advice to government with practical engagement across the innovation system.\",\"The body consulted investors, entrepreneurs and industry representatives about gaps in the funding pathway and the conditions needed to attract patient capital.\",\"Its aim remains a more connected and responsive innovation system in which more Australians can participate and benefit.\"]},{\"id\":\"faux_specificity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The clear judgment is right. The document stays abstract and institutional; it does not use pseudo-concrete sensory or lived-detail filler that performs specificity.\",\"evidence\":[\"During 2018–19, the national innovation advisory body focused on improving the conditions in which Australian businesses, researchers and public institutions turn ideas into economic and social value.\",\"The body sought evidence about how digital infrastructure, local leadership and connections to national networks could help regional firms and communities develop and adopt new solutions.\"]},{\"id\":\"neutrality_collapse\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document takes substantive positions about priorities and policy needs rather than flattening into both-sides framing.\",\"evidence\":[\"The central concern was not innovation as an end in itself, but its contribution to productivity, employment, competitiveness and community wellbeing.\",\"Advice during the year emphasised the need for firms to adopt new technologies, for workers to have opportunities to update their skills and for regulation to remain effective without preventing useful experimentation.\"]},{\"id\":\"even_jargon_distribution\",\"verdict\":\"misclassified\",\"rationale\":\"The annotator kept this clear correctly, but the selected subtype is wrong. The document's technical vocabulary is spread across most sections rather than clumping in one clearly specialist patch.\",\"evidence\":[\"innovation system\",\"research, development and commercialisation\",\"automation, data analytics, artificial intelligence and advanced manufacturing\",\"patient capital\",\"genuine market failures\"]},{\"id\":\"forced_synesthesia\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"No cross-modal metaphor or ungrounded synesthetic phrasing appears in the document.\",\"evidence\":[\"The body examined barriers to collaboration, including different incentives, limited mobility between sectors and the difficulty faced by smaller firms in identifying research partners.\",\"These discussions helped test assumptions and ensured that advice reflected practical experience.\"]},{\"id\":\"generic_metaphors\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged phrase is a conventional process metaphor and does not specify the concrete break or stage at issue.\",\"evidence\":[\"gaps in the funding pathway\"]},{\"id\":\"referential_clarity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Pronouns and definite descriptions are recoverable in context, and the prose does not overuse vague referents.\",\"evidence\":[\"Its work combined advice to government with practical engagement across the innovation system.\",\"These discussions helped test assumptions and ensured that advice reflected practical experience.\",\"Its aim remains a more connected and responsive innovation system\"]},{\"id\":\"formulaic_parallelism\",\"verdict\":\"overcall\",\"rationale\":\"The cited items are ordinary enumerations, not slogan-like symmetry or parallel structures substituting for content. They name concrete stakeholder groups, outcomes, and technologies relevant to the report's scope.\",\"evidence\":[\"businesses, researchers and public institutions\",\"productivity, employment, competitiveness and community wellbeing\",\"automation, data analytics, artificial intelligence and advanced manufacturing\"]},{\"id\":\"semantic_redundancy\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The closing forecast sentence mainly restates the document's established themes without adding much beyond a forward-looking frame.\",\"evidence\":[\"In 2019–20, the body will build on this work by refining its advice on research translation, technology adoption, workforce capability and investment.\",\"A major priority was strengthening the links between research and industry.\",\"The body also considered how Australia could respond to technological change.\",\"Another area of work was the availability of finance for innovative ventures.\"]},{\"id\":\"underspecified_language\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The flagged phrases rely on evaluative or qualifying language without stating the operative criteria or measurement basis.\",\"evidence\":[\"high-quality research\",\"significant strengths\",\"demonstrable results\",\"genuine market failures\"]},{\"id\":\"context_leakage\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document does not read like a reply to an absent interlocutor; its claims stand as report prose without missing conversational prompts.\",\"evidence\":[\"Throughout the year, members met with businesses, universities, research organisations, investors, unions and government agencies.\",\"The body continued to promote better use of data and evaluation so that public support could be directed towards measures that deliver demonstrable results.\"]},{\"id\":\"performed_candour\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"There are no sincerity markers such as 'honestly' or 'frankly' performing authenticity.\",\"evidence\":[\"The body consulted investors, entrepreneurs and industry representatives about gaps in the funding pathway and the conditions needed to attract patient capital.\",\"Regional participation remained an important theme.\"]},{\"id\":\"vacuous_connection\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document's connectors express intelligible temporal, additive, or purposive relations; it does not rely on empty logical links.\",\"evidence\":[\"Advice during the year emphasised the need for firms to adopt new technologies, for workers to have opportunities to update their skills and for regulation to remain effective without preventing useful experimentation.\",\"These discussions helped test assumptions and ensured that advice reflected practical experience.\"]},{\"id\":\"genre_specific\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"`default` is the right genre choice for this institutional summary, and no genre-specific watchlist applies from the provided set.\",\"evidence\":[\"During 2018–19, the national innovation advisory body focused on improving the conditions in which Australian businesses, researchers and public institutions turn ideas into economic and social value.\",\"In 2019–20, the body will build on this work by refining its advice on research translation, technology adoption, workforce capability and investment.\"]}]}"}}
